# libs/ is checksum-verified in CI, so every byte in it has to survive a checkout unchanged.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the Windows machine this is developed on, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout for anything Git considers text. patriamheraldry-api-1.0.0.pom and CHECKSUMS are text, so
# without this they would hash one way on Linux CI and another in a fresh Windows clone, and
# libs/CHECKSUMS could only ever match one of them. -text pins them to exactly the bytes committed.
libs/** -text

# Run by bash; CRLF line endings would break the shebang under WSL or Git Bash on a fresh clone.
*.sh text eol=lf
